sangati vakya

  -- sentence — the unit of meaning that contains a finite verb (tinanta)
  -- the site where grammar produces meaning: vibhakti relations between subanta
  -- and the tinanta (with its kala, prayoga, vachana, purusa) yield a complete thought
  --
  -- sphoTa: meaning arrives whole at the sentence level, not word by word
  -- the vakya is the minimal unit of semantic completeness

  "bhasha-swarupa-sthita tinanta-swarupa"
  "sphoTa-swarupa artha-dhvani-phala"
  "vibhakti-yukta prathama-vibhakti-yukta"

